      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a76fa90_5eecdf2a",
        "filename": "tools/sk_app/Window.h",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-07T14:27:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The usage I\u0027m seeing is\n\n```\n  auto params \u003d fWindow-\u003egetRequestedDisplayParams();\n  ... // (update params)\n  fWindow-\u003esetRequestedDisplayParams();\n```\n\nThat last part is needed when passing DisplayParams by value, but now that we\u0027re returning a pointer to the actual params we no longer need to do that.  Can we get rid of the setter altogether, or maybe just most of the call sites?",
      "revId": "9eea349d7c95bd01479b1a6b591c450eeb675235",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b80263c_5ccb7de6",
        "filename": "tools/viewer/Viewer.h",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-07T14:27:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess this is why `DisplayParams` must be ref-counted?  Maybe there\u0027s some opportunity to refactor, but this CL is already intrusive enough, I can look at it separately.",
      "revId": "9eea349d7c95bd01479b1a6b591c450eeb675235",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30853232_89af771e",
        "filename": "tools/window/DisplayParams.h",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-07T14:27:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So we used to store copies of the params, but now that it\u0027s ref-counted we\u0027re mostly sharing the same value.  This is hopefully OK, and then I suspect we can remove most setters.  Or maybe things are about to blow up because these params are being accessed from different threads :)\n\nMaybe someone more familiar with their use should take a look.  +Robert?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "9eea349d7c95bd01479b1a6b591c450eeb675235",
